                <pb facs="0501" n="385" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg385"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 738.3915/126.]</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1912-07-01">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 1, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">[Memorandum of the fourth meeting.]</p>
                <p>Pursuant to agreement, the plenipotentiaries of Haiti and the Dominican Republic
                    met at the Department of State on July 1, 1912, at 11:00 a.m. The Dominican
                    Minister thereupon stated that he had received a draft protocol prepared by the
                    Minister of Haiti shortly after the last meeting, and having read it had certain
                    observations which he desired to make regarding it. These he submitted in
                    writing, in Spanish, saying that it would not be possible for him to express
                    himself in English or French with sufficient accuracy with regard thereto.</p>
                <p>Mr. Peynado thereupon submitted a draft protocol in Spanish, which he proposed
                    should be agreed to.</p>
                <p>The plenipotentiaries thereupon determined that, as it would take some time for
                    the Haitian Minister to study the Dominican Minister’s draft, adjournment should
                    be taken until 11:30 o’clock Saturday, July 6th.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Doyle.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
